    "title": "UFC 320 full fight: Alex Pereira ices Jamahal Hill in iconic KO win - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By MMA Junkie ,\n3 hours ago\nOne of Alex Pereira's best highlight reel moments came in one of the UFC's biggest events ever.\nBack at UFC 300 in 2024, Pereira put the lights out on bitter rival and former UFC champion Jamahal Hill in style. After taking an accidental illegal groin kick, Pereira stopped the referee from intervening, pushing him aside, and then delivered a left hook from hell that sent Hill crashing down to the canvas. Only a few more shots were needed after the knockdown to lock in his first title defense as light heavyweight champion.\nYou can watch Pereira's signature win in the video above.\nPereira (12-3 MMA, 9-2 UFC) returns to the cage this Saturday in the main event of UFC 320 at T-Mobile Arena in Las Vegas. He takes on Magomed Ankalaev (21-1-1 MMA, 12-1-1 UFC) in an immediate rematch after losing his belt to the Russian fighter in March.\nThis article originally appeared on MMA Junkie: UFC 320 full fight: Alex Pereira ices Jamahal Hill in iconic KO win\n1",
